course: dictionary
lesson: 270
title: When a sentence can mean two things
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words and sentences can be read in two different ways. We call these ambiguous. Ambiguous means having more than one possible meaning, so you cannot tell straight away which one the writer wants.
explain: Look at «I saw a man on a hill with a telescope.» Who has the telescope? It could be you, or it could be the man. The sentence is ambiguous because both readings fit the words.
explain: Writers avoid ambiguity by changing the word order or adding commas. Ambiguous can also mean uncertain, as in an ambiguous answer or an ambiguous ending that leaves you guessing.
fact: Ambiguous is an adjective: ambiguous, more ambiguous, most ambiguous.
fact: «Ambiguous» means having more than one possible meaning.
fact: An ambiguous sentence can be understood in two or more ways.
fact: In maths, a question is ambiguous if it can be read in two ways, so mathematicians use brackets.
fact: A pronoun is ambiguous when it could point to more than one person.
exercise: «I saw a man on a hill with a telescope.» Why is this sentence ambiguous? | It has no verb in it | It is written as a question | *It could mean you had the telescope or the man had it | Hill is a silly word
exercise: In maths, how can you make an ambiguous question clear? | Use no numbers at all | Write the whole question in capital letters | *Use brackets to show the order of the steps | Make the question shorter
exercise: What does an ambiguous ending do? | Has no words in it | *Leaves you unsure what really happened | Is always a happy ending | Tells you exactly what happened
test: Which word means having more than one possible meaning? | Simple | *Ambiguous | Clear | Certain
test: «Sam told Leo that he had won.» Who might «he» mean? | Only a telescope | The teacher who wrote the story | *Sam or Leo
exam: Which is the best way to remove ambiguity from a sentence? | Make it longer with no punctuation | *Change the word order or add commas to show the meaning | Use a word that has two meanings | Write it in a different language
